WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.737
A useful monitoring pattern is to compare the live result with the stored snapshot.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:08.532
This query shows diagnosis counts from both sources.

00:00:08.532 --> 00:00:12.977
After a successful refresh, the values should agree for the same logic.

00:00:12.977 --> 00:00:19.397
If they differ unexpectedly, investigate whether the snapshot is stale or the definitions are inconsistent.

00:00:19.397 --> 00:00:25.442
A materialized view stores the query result physically, trading freshness for faster reads.

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.897
That makes refresh policy part of the data contract.

00:00:28.897 --> 00:00:33.872
A dashboard should know whether the snapshot is five minutes old or one day old.

00:00:33.872 --> 00:00:39.132
Indexes can improve access, and concurrent refresh has additional requirements.
